    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d570">

                <pb facs="1093" n="1049" xml:id="pg1049"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.5/8–1854</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Prime Minister Churchill
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d570-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1954-08-18">August 18,
                        1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir Winston</hi>: I returned yesterday from a weekend vacation
                    and found your kind message.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d570-f2"/> I am honored and
                    heartened that you occasionally follow the low-level of the Foreign Office and
                    not merely the summits.</p>
                <p>I am glad that we are following a common line as regards Mendes-France. I agree with you that
                    it is time to bring this chapter to an end. I hope that it will be an EDC ending. I am not clear in my mind as to any
                    alternative which will be both practical and not subject to another succession
                    of parliamentary wrangles.</p>
                <p>Our papers fully report the Attlee-Bevan excursion
                    with many pictures. From our standpoint they do not make a helpful exhibit. I
                    fear we can only exchange condolences on the subject of your last sentence.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Foster Dulles</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d570-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d570-f1-content">
                <p>Transmitted to London in telegram 984, Aug. 18, with instructions to the
                    Ambassador to deliver to the Prime Minister.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d570-f2" n="2" xml:id="d570-f2-content">
                <p>Presumably the message of Aug. 14, <ref target="#pg1037">p. 1037</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
